# Patterns to ignore when building packages (same syntax as .gitignore, but see the note below).

# A chart packaged from inside this directory (`helm package .`) writes server-<version>.tgz here. Left in, the next `helm package`
# packs it into the chart, and the release Helm stores in a Secret grows past Kubernetes' 1 MiB limit ("Secret ... is invalid: data:
# Too long"). Named after the chart rather than `*.tgz` or `/*.tgz`: Helm doesn't anchor a leading slash, so those also match the
# dependency archives under charts/, and packaging then fails with "missing in charts/ directory".
/server-*.tgz

# Version control and editor leftovers.
.git/
.gitignore
.DS_Store
*.swp
*.bak
*.tmp
*~
.vscode/
.idea/
